  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A six-place number is formed by repeating a three-place number; for example, \\(256{,}256,\\) or \\(678{,}678,\\) etc. Any number of this form is always exactly divisible by:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(7\\) only"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(11\\) only"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(13\\) only"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(101\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(1001\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "1001"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1951-p19.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If the repeated block is \\(N,\\) then the six-place number is \\[ 1000N+N=1001N. \\] It is therefore always divisible by \\(1001.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Represent the repeated three-digit block by \\(N\\)",
        "The six-digit number is \\(1000N+N\\)"
      ],
